# Mechanics evaluation reports

When the user asks to create, open, or rebuild an athlete mechanics report (or gives an athlete name + stills path), follow `.cursor/skills/mechanics-evaluation-report/SKILL.md`.

Reports are a **local CLI** in this repo (`tools/mechanics-report/`). Do not invent a new template or wire the React/Go app for this yet.

```bash
python3 tools/mechanics-report/new_report.py create \
  --athlete "Jane Doe" \
  --stills "/absolute/path/to/stills" \
  --serve
```

Example user ask: "Generate a report for Jane Doe. Stills are in ~/Downloads/jane."

Rules:
- One folder per athlete: `templates/reports/<slug>/` (stills, `notes.json`, HTML).
- NPA only. Do not use Tom House language.
- Do not draft coach cues unless the user provides them.
- If still mapping fails, stop and ask. Pass `--map` or rename files.
- Reopen with `python3 tools/mechanics-report/new_report.py serve --slug <slug>`.
- Ben Staples is the filled example. Do not wipe `templates/reports/ben-staples/notes.json`.
